[recv] {"type": "message_start", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_DNjevFs0nDJ4GYYlrNs7JhAQ|fc_0aae1c8da5179779016ac62d81579c87d18a07f0ece5748e42", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "### Human intervention needed\n\nThe automated job failed in `explore/generate_tests()` while handling reporter-requested metadata. Preserved work: https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/tree/ai%2Fkimeta%2Fhuman-intervention%2Fissue-9730-library-new-request-org.springframework.boot-spring-boot-micrometer-metrics-test-4.1.1-0e0886d2\n\nThe likely blocker is Spring Test AOT handling. The latest Gradle run built the native image, but all 4 tests failed at runtime with `ClassNotFoundException: org.springframework.test.context.aot.AotTestContextInitializers__Generated`. The metadata agent then made no change because the issue body requested no specific metadata and classified this generated class as test infrastructure rather than library metadata. An earlier checkpoint did pass 5/5 native tests, indicating that a later test variant or stale Gradle/native output introduced the failure. Metrics ended as `failure` after 12 iterations with finalization still pending and no coverage result; dynamic-access reporting also failed because its output directory was not produced.\n\nInspect:\n- `human-intervention-logs/org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-micrometer-metrics-test:4.1.1/gradle-test/gradle-test-2026-10-07T05-24-36-243697Z.log`\n- `human-intervention-logs/org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-micrometer-metrics-test:4.1.1/issue-requested-metadata/pi.log`\n- `human-intervention-logs/org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-micrometer-metrics-test:4.1.1/native-test-verify/cycle-0-finalizedTest-2026-10-07T04-53-50-525887Z.log`\n- `human-intervention-logs/org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-micrometer-metrics-test:4.1.1/gradle/generateDynamicAccessCoverageReport-2026-10-07T05-04-52-350867Z.log`\n\nManual next steps:\n1. Compare checkpoint `b806c425826b829eb140e9bb9677215f475ae75f` with the later failing test variant and retain the 5-test implementation that passed native verification.\n2. Clean the coordinate’s build outputs and rerun its full test task; if `TestContextManager` remains necessary, wire Spring Test AOT generation into the test setup rather than adding unrelated hand-written metadata.\n3. Regenerate the dynamic-access coverage report and metrics after native tests pass.\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1791372675106}}
